      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "ed43837a-01fa-5800-9679-fb85a162cdcc",
        ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e82,-3,4\u27e9$, $b=\u27e85,k,-7\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e8-2,8,3\u27e9$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "91291cbc-08f4-56aa-87cc-f8a1457cae9d",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "e0716d2f-8a65-525d-bb2d-20b4c708ff9b",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "-\\frac{275}{14}"
              }
            ],
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "e0716d2f-8a65-525d-bb2d-20b4c708ff9b"
            ]
          }
        ],
        ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & k & -7 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -7 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((2)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (3)-(-7)\\cdot (8)))+((3)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (3)-(-7)\\cdot (-2)))+((4)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (8)-(k)\\cdot (-2)))\\\\ &=((2)\\cdot (3k+56))+((3)\\cdot (1))+((4)\\cdot (2k+40))\\\\ &=(6k+112)+(3)+(8k+160)\\\\ &=14k+275\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14k+275&=0\\\\ 14k&=-275\\\\ k&=-\\frac{275}{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{275}{14}.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
      },
